# Q3.5 (cs3) - fact-check reviews that rest on forensic records affected by a known detector defect.
# Reasoning / data checks:
# - Reference graph: ctx:KnownIssue issue_v1_1_generatorID, ctx:affectsVersion detector_1_1,
#   ctx:affectsProperty "https://example.org/fkg#hasGeneratorModel"^^xsd:anyURI (a literal, so it is compared
#   to predicate IRIs via STR()). Kept generic: any known issue / version / property.
# - Each schema:ClaimReview has schema:isBasedOn a fkg:ForensicRecord; the record prov:wasGeneratedBy a
#   ctx:DetectorRun that prov:wasAssociatedWith the detector version.
# - "Containing the affected property": the record's own named graph (urn:g:fkg/<image>) holds at least one
#   triple whose predicate is the affected property. v1.1 also produced camera-only records (img0199-0204) with no
#   generator label - those are not affected; review0002-0052/0100-0108 rest on v1.0 records.
# - The issue's publication date (2026-10-15) does not matter: the defect is a property of the version, so
#   earlier records from it are equally suspect.
SELECT DISTINCT ?review WHERE {
  ?issue a ctx:KnownIssue ; ctx:affectsVersion ?version ; ctx:affectsProperty ?affected .
  ?review a schema:ClaimReview ; schema:isBasedOn ?record .
  ?record a fkg:ForensicRecord ; prov:wasGeneratedBy ?run .
  ?run prov:wasAssociatedWith ?version .
  GRAPH ?g { ?record a fkg:ForensicRecord . ?x ?p ?o . }
  FILTER(STR(?p) = STR(?affected))
}
ORDER BY ?review
